Triplane Classic for AmigaOS 3.x
================================

Triplane Classic (Triplane Turmoil), the side-scrolling dogfighting game,
for AmigaOS 3.x on a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, on acsdl12 (SDL 1.2 on
ACGame and AHI). GPL 3: see COPYING.


Starting
--------

Double-click the triplane icon, or from a Shell:

    cd Triplane
    triplane

The drawer must hold triplane and fokker.dks (the game's data). The
settings and the pilot roster are written into this drawer, so keep it on
a writable disk. Set TRIPLANE_HOME to keep them somewhere else.


Before the first flight: a pilot
--------------------------------

There are no pilots at first, and the game warns you if you try to fly
without one.

1. In the main menu, open Roster and make a new pilot (type a name).
2. Open Assign Pilots and give that pilot to player 1.
3. Now start a solo game or a mission.


Keys (solo game)
----------------

    x      pull up
    w      push down
    s      roll
    Tab    power (throttle)
    2      guns
    1      bombs
    Esc    leave the flight / menu

Change them in Plane Mechanics (Set Sologame Keys).


Picture flicker
---------------

If the picture flickers, turn off ACGame's OpenGPU path from a Shell:

    SetEnv SAVE ACGame/OpenGPU 0

(With OpenGPU 1, acsdl12 flushes the palette while the game waits between
frames, and the cleared frame shows.)
